  "title": "A knot hides at most one bit from its pairs, and a network at most one bit per cycle, filled only by parity",
  "subject": "How much a system of constraints on bits hides from its pairs, and how that adds up",
  "conclusion": "The bits a relation on bits hides from its pairs vanish exactly at two-literal clauses, reach one bit only for parity among knots, reach about n - log2 log2 n on n bits through covering arrays, and the statistical version vanishes only on least sets of pairwise energies, so not-all-equal is the only silent knot. With hidden joints, a network of knots hides at most one bit per independent cycle, exactly for parity, and frustrating patches add up.",
